# API server base URL for production builds.
#
# Leave unset (or empty) for same-origin deployments — the frontend will issue
# relative /api/... requests. This is the default when served behind a reverse
# proxy or via the Vite dev proxy (vite.config.ts maps /api → localhost:8080).
#
# Set to an absolute URL for cross-origin deployments (e.g. static frontend on
# a CDN pointing at a separately hosted API server). The Go API server must
# allow the frontend's origin via --frontend-url for CORS to succeed.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# Notes:
#   - Trailing slashes are stripped at module init time.
#   - During `npm run dev`, setting VITE_API_BASE_URL bakes the absolute URL
#     into the running frontend code, so every API call is absolute/cross-
#     origin and the Vite dev proxy is effectively bypassed. Make sure the
#     Go server has --frontend-url set to the dev-server origin (e.g.
#     http://localhost:3000) so CORS preflight succeeds.

# Expose deterministic testing-only AI backends in backend selectors.
# Leave unset in normal builds.
#
#   VITE_SHOW_TESTING_BACKENDS=true
